# Editing Claude Code config files

These files configure Anthropic's Claude Code CLI. They are NOT application
source code and have NO runtime in this repo. When you touch them, follow these
rules exactly.

## CLAUDE.md
- MUST stay under 200 lines. If it grows past that, move detail into a separate
  file and reference it with `@path/to/file`.
- Keep it factual: stack, run/test commands, conventions, and model/effort/
  context-hygiene rules. No marketing prose, no emoji.
- Use strong imperative language ("ALWAYS", "NEVER"), not "prefer" or "try to".

## Slash commands — critical
- NEVER invent slash commands. Only these built-ins exist:
  `/model`, `/effort`, `/context`, `/compact`, `/clear`, `/cost`, `/usage`,
  `/stats`, `/plan`, `/resume`, `/rewind`, `/export`, `/agents`, `/mcp`,
  `/permissions`, `/memory`, `/help`.
- Commands like `/summarize`, `/session-switch`, `/token-status` do NOT exist.
  Do not reference them.
- Custom commands are real ONLY when defined as a markdown file in
  `.claude/commands/<name>.md`; invoking one is `/<name>`.

## .claude/settings.json
- MUST be valid JSON. Validate before saving.
- `model`: one of `"sonnet"`, `"opus"`, `"haiku"`, `"opusplan"`, `"default"`.
- `effort`: one of `"low"`, `"medium"`, `"high"`, `"max"` (`max` is Opus-only).
- Force one model for all subagents via `env.CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL`.
- To hard-cap cost, set `availableModels` to exclude `"opus"`.

## .claude/commands/<name>.md (custom commands)
- Frontmatter may include `description` and `argument-hint`.
- Body is the instruction Claude runs. Keep it tight and end by telling it not
  to restate the instructions.

## .claude/agents/<name>.md (subagents)
- Frontmatter fields: `name`, `description`, optional `model:`, optional `tools:`.
- Pin read-heavy/verbose agents to a cheap model so their output stays out of
  the main context window.

## Token-efficiency intent (preserve when editing)
- Every Claude Code message re-sends full history as input, so the config exists
  to keep history small: clear/compact often, route to the cheapest capable
  model, push verbose reads into subagents, and disable unused MCP servers.
- NEVER add an MCP server or new dependency to the config unless explicitly asked.

## When unsure
- Re-read the actual file before editing rather than assuming its contents.
- If a requested change would break one of the rules above, say so instead of doing it.
